# Synopsis

## Title

**AI-Powered Smart City Issue Reporting Platform**

## Introduction

Smart cities aim to provide efficient public services and improve the quality of life for citizens. However, issues such as potholes, overflowing garbage bins, water leakages, damaged streetlights, and broken roads are often reported manually through phone calls or paper-based complaints, leading to delays and lack of transparency. This project proposes an AI-powered web platform that enables citizens to report civic issues quickly and allows government authorities to monitor, prioritize, and resolve them efficiently.

## Problem Statement

Existing complaint management systems often suffer from slow response times, duplicate complaints, improper categorization, and limited tracking capabilities. Citizens frequently do not know which department is responsible for their issue, and authorities struggle to prioritize complaints based on urgency.

## Proposed Solution

The proposed system is a full-stack web application that uses Artificial Intelligence to automatically analyze uploaded images of civic problems. Citizens can report issues by uploading a photo, selecting or confirming the location, and adding a brief description. The AI model identifies the type of issue, estimates its severity, and routes it to the appropriate municipal department. Authorities can monitor complaints through an interactive dashboard, assign tasks, update statuses, and analyze trends using maps and visual reports.

## Objectives

* Develop an online platform for reporting civic issues.
* Automatically classify reported problems using AI.
* Detect the severity of reported issues to assist prioritization.
* Route complaints to the appropriate government department.
* Provide real-time complaint tracking for citizens.
* Offer an administrative dashboard with analytics and reports.
* Reduce complaint resolution time and improve transparency.

